{#
    Sign in. The Twig delivery's front door, and the page ADR 008's stateful firewall exists for.

    THE DESIGN SYSTEM HAS NO LOGIN COMPONENT. That is a real gap and it is reported rather than
    filled: this page invents no class name at all, and is assembled from three partials that
    already exist (`forms/Field`, `moments/Button`, `moments/Notice`) plus the layout classes
    `.page`, `.stack` and `.stack-6` from `styles.css`. If a `Login` component is drawn later, this
    file collapses into it and nothing in `styles.css` has to be unpicked first.

    Two smaller gaps in `forms/Field`, met here and worth naming for whoever draws that component:
    it cannot carry `required`, nor an `autocomplete` token, and a sign-in form wants
    `autocomplete="username"` and `autocomplete="current-password"` so a password manager can fill
    it. Overriding the partial's `control` block from this page would copy the component's markup
    into a page, which is the one thing "one component, one partial" forbids, so the attributes are
    absent and the gap is written down.

    THE IDENTIFIER IS A USERNAME, AND IT IS NEITHER THE HANDLE NOR A ULID. ADR 009 rule 10: a
    credential is identified by something a human typed. This field used to ask for a member's ULID,
    which is ADR 007 rule 9 with a form around it, because a ULID is on no screen and in no password
    manager. `Credential`'s docblock argues the rest: not the handle, because a handle is
    renameable (membership/03) and a user identifier that changes when somebody edits their profile is
    a session that silently belongs to nobody; and a username rather than an email address, because
    an address needs verifying, changes, feeds a recovery flow nothing here can perform, and is
    personal data the erasure saga would then owe an erasure of.

    THE FAILURE IS SYMFONY'S, IN SYMFONY'S WORDS. ADR 008 settles the debt ADR 007 left open: we do
    not re-render an authentication failure. It happens before any of our code runs, so there is no
    command, no handler and no domain exception; `messageKey` is translated from the `security`
    catalogue, in fifty-seven locales, and duplicating it into `failures` would be the second
    English ADR 007 rejected everywhere else. So no `FailureCode`, no catalogue entry, and
    `bin/console app:messages` counts exactly what it counted before this page.

    It lands in `moments/Notice` rather than on a field, for the reason that partial already gives
    about ADR 004's 400: "Invalid credentials." deliberately does not say which of the two was
    wrong, so there is no `propertyPath` to hang it from. A banner is the honest shape for a failure
    that belongs to the pair.

    CSRF. ADR 008 asks for it on every write form on the stateful firewall, and this is the first
    one. `form_login`'s defaults are the field name `_csrf_token` and the token id `authenticate`;
    they are spelled out below rather than configured away, because a reader comparing this file to
    `config/packages/security.php` should be able to see the two halves match.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Sign in{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <main class="page">
        <div class="stack-6" style="max-width:420px;margin:0 auto">
            <h1 class="display-md">Sign in</h1>

            {% if error %}
                {% include 'components/_notice.html.twig' with {
                    sentence: error.messageKey|trans(error.messageData, 'security'),
                    tone: 'danger',
                } only %}
            {% endif %}

            <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_login') }}" class="stack">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token('authenticate') }}">

                {% include 'components/_field.html.twig' with {
                    label: 'Username',
                    name: '_username',
                    hint: 'The name your credential was issued with. Not your handle, which you can change.',
                    value: last_username,
                } only %}

                {% include 'components/_field.html.twig' with {
                    label: 'Password',
                    name: '_password',
                    type: 'password',
                } only %}

                <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Sign in</button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </main>
{% endblock %}
